h {} "Judge #2"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/2305736"} "John Ammerman"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #3"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/2305705"} "Eryk Brabec"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #4"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/12623"} "Jaap Rijks"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Course Designer"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/2305738"} "Bertalan de Némethy"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The event was slightly different as the top 25 riders in round one, instead of 20, were advanced to the second round. The favorite was probably American " [:a {:href "/athletes/11460"} "Melanie Smith"] " who, aboard " [:a {:href "/horses/373"} "Calypso"] ", had led the 1982 World Cup and was third in 1983 behind her countryman " [:a {:href "/athletes/11870"} "Norman Dello Joio"] " and Austrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/12744"} "Hugo Simon"] ". The US team for Los Angeles was so strong that Dello Joio was not even selected for it, as they opted instead for " [:a {:href "/athletes/11951"} "Joe Fargis"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/12131"} "Conrad Homfeld"] ", who were stablemates in Petersburg, Virginia."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Fargis led round one with a clean trip, tied with Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12997"} "Michael Whitaker"] ", while Holmfeld and Smith were in a five-way tie for third with 4.00 faults. Holmfeld then posted a clean ride in round two for a total of 4.00 faults. Fargis rode cleanly in his second round, until the final barrier, on which his horse, " [:a {:href "/horses/2494"} "Touch of Class"] ", knocked over the top rail. Fargis and Holmfeld thus tied with 4.00 faults and would have to jump-off. Fargis won the gold medal with another perfect round, leaving Holmfeld with silver."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Smith dropped back in round two and tied for seventh, but Whitaker had a disastrous ride, with 28.50 faults, and placed 24th. The bronze came down to a jump-off among Switzerland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/11444"} "Heidi Robbiani"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/11719"} "Bruno Candrian"] ", Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/11875"} "Mario Deslauriers"] ". Robbiani secured third-place with a clean ride in the jump-off, as Deslauriers placed fourth with 4 faults, and Candrian had 8 faults."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Faults"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "183"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11951"} "Joe Fargis"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2494"} "Touch of Class"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "4.00"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "186"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12131"} "Conrad Homfeld"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/6"} "Abdullah"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :sr